    "statement": "Assume full AC. There exist universal $\\epsilon,C>0$ such that every smooth $\\mathfrak{su}(2)$ connection form $A$ on $B_2(0)\\setminus\\{0\\}\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ with Euclidean $F_A^+=0$ and $\\|F_A\\|_{L^2(B_2\\setminus\\{0\\})}\\le\\epsilon$ admits a smooth gauge $g:B_{1/2}\\setminus\\{0\\}\\to SU(2)$ for which\n$$B=A^g\\in L^4(B_{1/2}),\\qquad \\|B\\|_{L^4(B_{1/2})}\\le C\\|F_A\\|_{L^2(B_2)},\\qquad \\|F_B\\|_{L^2(B_{1/2})}\\le\\|F_A\\|_{L^2(B_2)}.$$\nThe singleton has measure zero in these norms; no value of $B$ at zero is prescribed. The input includes only finite small curvature energy and the punctured ASD equation, not an assumed small potential gauge. No Coulomb condition or smooth extension across zero is asserted by this lemma.",
    "raw_sha256": "533c1018fab9bede500a9894bca100b4f82ac91243f4312e68deb7415f3f2ecd"
  },
